     "style": "methode",
     "title": "Unlike denominators",
     "md": "To add or subtract fractions with **different denominators**, first change them to the **same denominator** (use the LCM). $\\frac{1}{2} + \\frac{1}{4}$: change $\\frac{1}{2}$ to $\\frac{2}{4}$, then $\\frac{2}{4} + \\frac{1}{4} = \\frac{3}{4}$. Add or subtract the numerators; keep the denominator."
